why do humans return to Pandora in  avatar The Way of water is it for more  unobtainium James Cameron might just  surprise you at its core the Avatar  franchise is an outlandish science  fiction fantasy with its bizarre Bevy of  colorful creatures and Fantastical  Vistas the world of Pandora undeniably  Embraces its strange Concepts and finds  exciting ways to expand upon them  continuously however the franchise's way  of presenting these Larger than Life  ideas alongside its social commentary  remains most intriguing even if it's far  from the first sci-fi flick to do this  one of these attempts to connect the  franchise's wondrous settings to a real  world dilemma is with the special  Compound on obtainium in the first  avatar we learned that unoptanium acts  as a powerful superconductor which those  on Earth seek to use as a power source  given the energy crisis they are  experiencing however the navi people  forbid the mining of it as they view the  Tree of Souls where it's located as a  sacred place the environmental metaphor  may be pretty on the nose but it's  nevertheless an integral part of the  story Avatar tries to tell about our  inner connection with nature and how far  we are willing to fight for it I'm a  warrior like you I'm supposed to fight  it's all the more surprising that film  sequel Avatar the way of water never  mentions unobtainium that's right the  very element that caused the central  conflict in Pandora's history is not  given a single mention in the way of  water so what does the absence of this  crucial substance mean for the greater  Avatar story moving forward the term  unobtainium is not present in avatar The  Way of water but that doesn't mean the  idea behind the substance is lost the  film sees Colonel Miles courage return  in an avatar body to take down Jake  Sully and his family when Sully decides  to move his family beyond the outskirts  of their Forest Home they join the  mechano tribe of the ocean who teaches  the family their ways amongst the most  crucial aspects of the metcina way of  life comes their connection with the  whale-like creatures The Tokens The  People hold the intelligent creatures in  extremely high regard seeing them as  siblings and forming lifelong  connections with the animals from birth  in an attempt by courage and his band of  goons to lure Sully from hiding they  team up with a ship of Tolkien Hunters  who help kill the animal to cause  distress to the Medina clap however  after killing the animals The Hunters  drill into their heads and take out a  Gloppy liquid that is incredibly  valuable with even a small canister  worth millions in this way the tolkiens  stand in as a similar piece of symbolism  that the unobtainium did in the first  film as a precious natural resource that  Humanity seeks to exploit it serves the  message here but even more significantly  it paints a picture of what we can  expect in the franchise's future the  seemingly forgotten unobtanium might  confuse viewers coming into Avatar the  way of water as an essential plot point  in the first film it seems natural that  this long-awaited sequel finds new ways  to expand and build upon what we already  know about the valuable substance but  just as the wave water explores new and  exciting lands in Pandora instead of  staying in the same places as  predecessor the film chooses to evolve  its thematic nature as well this family  is our Fortress keep in mind that the  way of water takes place more than a  decade after the first film's events in  that time the energy crisis on Earth has  likely taken over or if not is very  close to doing so is unobtainium still  strong enough to solve the issue even if  it proves powerful it's more than likely  that Colonel korich and this gang will  find similarly valuable resources  throughout Pandora and find some way to  exploit them for their own use the war  against humanity is about more than  protecting the navi people and the life  on Pandora but the 